# SyOS apt manifest - one package per line, '#' starts a comment.
# Every entry here was checked against Debian 13 (trixie) before landing.
# Google Chrome is NOT listed: it comes from Google's own apt repo, which
# bootstrap.sh adds separately.

# --- Compositor and shell ----------------------------------------------
sway
swaybg
swayidle
xwayland
foot
waybar
fuzzel
mako-notifier

# --- Login / session ----------------------------------------------------
# greetd is the display manager; tuigreet is its terminal greeter. Both are
# in trixie, so the agetty-autologin fallback in the build plan is not used.
greetd
tuigreet

# --- Audio --------------------------------------------------------------
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
pavucontrol

# --- Desktop portals ----------------------------------------------------
# xdg-desktop-portal-wlr is what makes Chrome screen sharing work on Sway;
# the gtk portal supplies the file chooser that -wlr does not implement.
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk

# --- Authentication -----------------------------------------------------
# Without a running polkit agent, privileged prompts fail with no visible
# explanation at all.
polkitd
lxpolkit

# --- Fonts --------------------------------------------------------------
# Iosevka is not packaged in trixie (see docs/decisions.md) and is fetched
# by bootstrap.sh. fonts-hack is the guaranteed monospace fallback so the
# system stays legible if that download fails.
fontconfig
fonts-hack
fonts-dejavu-core
fonts-noto-color-emoji

# --- Icons --------------------------------------------------------------
# The launcher renders an icon beside each application; without an icon theme
# installed the list is text only and much slower to scan.
papirus-icon-theme

# --- Config management --------------------------------------------------
stow
git
curl
ca-certificates
gnupg
unzip

# --- Built-in tools -----------------------------------------------------
# These are what the launcher is expected to find. An application that is
# listed on the bar or reachable from "+" but not installed is worse than one
# that is missing entirely: it looks broken rather than absent.
neovim

# syos-notes is a GTK4 application written in Python; these are its only
# dependencies, and both are stock Debian.
python3-gi
python3-gi-cairo
gir1.2-gtk-4.0

# yazi, the file manager, is NOT here: it is not packaged in trixie and is
# vendored from its upstream release by bootstrap.sh.
#
# flatpak is not here either. bootstrap.sh installs it on demand, only if
# packages-flatpak.list has an entry, so an empty list costs no disk.

# --- Session utilities --------------------------------------------------
wl-clipboard
grim
slurp
jq
brightnessctl
network-manager
dbus-user-session
libnotify-bin
xdg-utils
python3
